# Memory index

This file is a map, not a journal. At the start of a run, use the “Read when” column to open only relevant topic files.

| Memory | Read when | Summary | Updated |
| --- | --- | --- | --- |
| [`memories/{{TOPIC}}.md`](memories/{{TOPIC}}.md) | {{SPECIFIC_TRIGGER}} | {{ONE_LINE_SUMMARY}} | {{YYYY-MM-DD}} |

## Maintenance contract

- Keep one topic per `memories/<kebab-case-topic>.md` file.
- Index every topic file and keep every link valid.
- Update a topic's current truth instead of appending a chronological log; git retains history.
- Change the topic file and this index atomically.
- Store durable context only. Keep queues, cursors, locks, pending work, run status, and raw output in the designated external system.
- Never store credentials, secret values, private keys, sensitive personal data, or raw conversation transcripts.
